\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Hypergraph of the legal-pluralism logic. Three legal codes (Statutory, Religious, Customary) form three contexts. Yellow vertices are intertwining atoms: $\{a_1,a_2\}$ (forest clearing---prohibited under both statutory and religious law) and $\{a_4,a_6\}$ (commercial use---set apart by both customary and religious law). White vertices represent groupings specific to one code. The non-Boolean pasting reflects the impossibility of a single ``master code'' that respects all three systems' distinctions simultaneously.}}{11}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:legal}{{4}{11}{Hypergraph of the legal-pluralism logic. Three legal codes (Statutory, Religious, Customary) form three contexts. Yellow vertices are intertwining atoms: $\{a_1,a_2\}$ (forest clearing---prohibited under both statutory and religious law) and $\{a_4,a_6\}$ (commercial use---set apart by both customary and religious law). White vertices represent groupings specific to one code. The non-Boolean pasting reflects the impossibility of a single ``master code'' that respects all three systems' distinctions simultaneously}{figure.4}{}}
