\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces The four organizational states arranged in a $2\times 2$ grid. The financial audit (directive~$a$, {\color  {ctxA}red dashed}) partitions the grid horizontally: it reveals the row (financial health) but conflates columns (compliance status). The operational inspection (directive~$b$, {\color  {ctxB}blue dotted}) partitions vertically: it reveals the column but conflates rows. The two partitions share \emph  {no} atoms---this is maximal complementarity.}}{12}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:org_grid}{{5}{12}{The four organizational states arranged in a $2\times 2$ grid. The financial audit (directive~$a$, {\color {ctxA}red dashed}) partitions the grid horizontally: it reveals the row (financial health) but conflates columns (compliance status). The operational inspection (directive~$b$, {\color {ctxB}blue dotted}) partitions vertically: it reveals the column but conflates rows. The two partitions share \emph {no} atoms---this is maximal complementarity}{figure.5}{}}
